{"name":"Tiara Pink","hex":"#daa6cf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiara","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The three-tiered papal crown.","An ornamental coronet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn as a tiara.","To adorn with a tiara."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiara"},{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiara","blocks":[{"text":"A tiara is a head ornament adorned with jewels. Its origins date back to ancient Persia, from where it was later popularized by the Greco-Roman world. By the 18th century, the tiara had become fashionable in Europe as prestigious pieces of jewelry worn by women on formal occasions. The basic shape of the modern tiara is a semicircular base, usually made of gold, silver, or platinum, and richly decorated with gemstones, pearls, or cameos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/%C3%89vrard_e_fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_bapst%2C_diadema_della_duchessa_d%27anguoleme%2C_smeraldi%2C_diamanti%2C_oro_e_argento%2C_parigi_1819-20.jpg/330px-%C3%89vrard_e_fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_bapst%2C_diadema_della_duchessa_d%27anguoleme%2C_smeraldi%2C_diamanti%2C_oro_e_argento%2C_parigi_1819-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiara","wikidata":"Q749249"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb